WEBVTT

00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:12.454
Hi, friends. Gani here. This is Emotion Weather Report.

00:00:12.454 --> 00:00:16.909
Sit tall in your chair. Feet flat on the floor.

00:00:16.909 --> 00:00:19.581
Hands resting on your desk. Shoulders soft.

00:00:19.581 --> 00:00:22.254
Take one slow breath with me… and let it go.

00:00:22.254 --> 00:00:30.271
Feelings are a little like weather. They happen inside us, and they change.

00:00:30.271 --> 00:00:38.289
Some moments feel sunny. Some feel cloudy. Some feel stormy, or foggy, or calm and clear.

00:00:38.289 --> 00:00:43.634
A weather report does not judge the weather. It just says what is happening in the sky.

00:00:43.634 --> 00:00:47.197
Today you give your own weather report. Eyes closed, or eyes open — both work.

00:00:47.197 --> 00:00:56.106
Look at your inside sky, gently, like you are checking the weather through a window.

00:00:56.106 --> 00:01:02.342
Is it sunny in there? Cloudy? Is there rain, or wind, or a storm moving through?

00:01:02.342 --> 00:01:10.360
Maybe it is foggy — hard to see how you feel. Foggy is a weather, too.

00:01:10.360 --> 00:01:19.268
Whatever you find is just weather. Weather is never bad, and never wrong.

00:01:19.268 --> 00:01:29.068
Now say your report in your mind: right now, my inside weather is… and let the word come.

00:01:29.068 --> 00:01:34.413
Remember: you are the sky, not the storm. The sky stays. The weather moves.

00:01:34.413 --> 00:01:40.649
Pick one small comfort for this weather: one slow breath, shoulders dropping down…

00:01:40.649 --> 00:01:45.994
…or hands resting warm in your lap. One small comfort is enough.

00:01:45.994 --> 00:01:52.230
Weather always moves. Storms pass. Clouds drift. The sun comes back.

00:01:52.230 --> 00:01:59.357
That is your Emotion Weather Report. You can check your sky any time.

00:01:59.357 --> 00:02:02.029
Hands down. One more slow breath… and let it go.

00:02:02.029 --> 00:02:05.592
Eyes open. Look around your classroom.

00:02:05.592 --> 00:02:09.156
You're ready for what's next.
